<Legal locale="en" route="privacy" title="Privacy policy" description="What is processed when you visit the Nemo website: no cookies, no tracking, hosting by Cloudflare.">
  <p class="placeholder">Placeholder: the operator adds the controller details. The description of processing is a draft and not legal advice.</p>

  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>
    [PLACEHOLDER: name]<br />
    [PLACEHOLDER: address]<br />
    E-mail: [PLACEHOLDER: e-mail address]
  </p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website sets no cookies, uses no analytics and loads no scripts, fonts or content from third-party servers.</li>
    <li>Your light/dark theme choice is stored only in your browser (localStorage) and never transmitted.</li>
    <li>When the page is requested, the hosting provider processes technically necessary connection data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hosting (Cloudflare Pages)</h2>
  <p>
    The website is served by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA (in the EU: Cloudflare Germany GmbH, Rosental 7, 80331 Munich).
    When you visit, Cloudflare processes connection data such as IP address, time, requested address, browser identifier and transferred data volume to deliver the page
    and protect it against attacks. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in secure, fast operation). Cloudflare is certified under the EU-US Data
    Privacy Framework; standard contractual clauses apply in addition. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.
    [PLACEHOLDER: if Cloudflare Web Analytics is enabled, add a note that the cookieless statistics store no IP addresses.]
  </p>

  <h2>Downloads and links to GitHub</h2>
  <p>
    The download buttons lead directly to GitHub (GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA), where the app files are hosted, and to the
    source code at <a href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener">{REPO_URL}</a>. GitHub processes your data only once you click;
    see <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Support via Ko-fi</h2>
  <p>
    The “Support on Ko-fi” link leads to <a href={KOFI_URL} rel="noopener">Ko-fi</a> (Ko-fi Labs Ltd, United Kingdom), an external provider. This website itself
    processes no payment or contact data. What Ko-fi processes is described in <a href="https://more.ko-fi.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Ko-fi’s privacy policy</a>.
    [PLACEHOLDER: if supporter codes are sent by e-mail, describe that service: which data (e-mail address) is stored and for how long.]
  </p>

  <h2>The Nemo app</h2>
  <p>
    The app stores its data only on your device. It has no account and no service run by the operator; optional sync works only through a server you run yourself.
    Updates are downloaded from GitHub. This policy covers the website only.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and objection (Art. 15–21 GDPR), and the right to lodge a complaint
    with a supervisory authority. [PLACEHOLDER: name the competent German state data protection authority.]
  </p>

  <h2>What usually belongs here in Germany</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    For orientation, not legal advice: name and contact of the controller, processing by the hosting provider (server logs, legal basis, third-country transfer),
    every external service (here only via links: GitHub, Ko-fi), whether cookies or tracking are used, data subject rights and the supervisory authority. Last updated: [PLACEHOLDER: date].
  </p>
</Legal>
